;; What contract THIS repo claims. The workspace-level authority is
;; com-junkawasaki/root `manifest/repository-rules.edn` (ADR-2607299000) — this
;; file only declares which of its rules apply here, so a checker can verify the
;; claim instead of inferring it from the name.
{:repository/name "loop-ka-production"
 :repository/prefix "loop-"
 :repository/role :continuous-orchestrator

 :repository/must
 {:observe "loop-ka.observe — which channels are due for this slot, and the
            REASON each skipped one is not. 'Nothing ran last night' has more
            than one cause; an unreadable catalog and an exhausted one are
            distinguished because they render identically and mean opposites."
  :evaluate "loop-ka.evaluate — grade the producer's own :legs report. Does the
             episode actually contain generated images and narration, or did the
             pipeline degrade to something that merely plays?"
  :decide "loop-ka.decide — publish | hold | discard, from the grade plus the
           channel's phase and grants. :degraded never auto-publishes at any
           phase."
  :act "loop-ka.task — emit a task batch. Nothing is executed here."
  :record-evidence "loop-ka.ledger — one append-only record per run, carrying
                    the verdict, the decision and its reason, and the artifact
                    CIDs."}

 :repository/must-not
 {:own-domain-scoring-truth
  "This loop does not score craft. Quality has homes already (design-quality's
   fitness functions, the gen-quality ledger's ffprobe metrics). It answers only
   the question that had no home: did the generative legs run at all? That is
   read from the producer's :legs, never invented here."

  :bind-to-one-ci-provider
  "`plan` writes a plain data batch. murakumo's fleet task plane is the resident
   path because it already owns placement, slots, load admission and retry — but
   the same batch runs under launchd, or one channel at a time by hand."}

 :repository/also-not
 {:hold-a-publishing-key
  "The loop mints no CACAO and holds no seed. Each channel publishes under its
   own actor DID with its own key; the loop decides whether to ASK. That keeps
   the blast radius of this repo at 'scheduling', not 'identity'."}

 :repository/composition
 {:libraries ["kotoba-lang/murakumo-generation"]
  :producers ["cloud-itonami/dougaka-actor" "etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-minidrama"
              "cloud-itonami/dougaka-vector" "cloud-itonami/yukkuri"]
  :resident-runner "kotoba-lang/murakumo (task plane)"
  :human-surface "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-app (reads the ledger)"}}
